BLOCK|h1|1|Cluster-lang: Chapter 3 — Models & Object Orientation
BLOCK|p||Cluster-lang provides clean struct and class modeling using the `model` keyword.
BLOCK|hr||
BLOCK|h2|2|1. Defining Models
BLOCK|p||Models hold fields (properties) and methods:
BLOCK|code|python|model Address:
    city: string
    zipcode: int

model User:
    name: string
    address: box[Address]    // box pointer to Address model

    fn get_city() -> string:
        // Methods can access local fields
        if self.address == None:
            return "Unknown"
        return self.address.city
BLOCK|hr||
BLOCK|h2|2|2. Instantiating Models
BLOCK|p||To instantiate a model, use the `box` keyword (which wraps it in a unique-pointer heap allocation) or construct it inline:
BLOCK|code|python|// 1. Create a heap-allocated Address
addr := box Address(city="New York", zipcode=10001)

// 2. Pass it to a User instance (note the move semantics for boxes!)
user := box User(name="John", address=move(addr))
BLOCK|hr||
BLOCK|h2|2|3. Optional Chaining (`?.`)
BLOCK|p||To access fields or call methods on potentially null reference pointers without manual nested `if` statements, use the optional chaining (`?.`) operator:
BLOCK|code|python|// If user or user.address is None, this safely evaluates to None without crashing!
city_name := user?.address?.city
BLOCK|p||If any reference along the chain evaluates to `None`, the execution stops and evaluates to `None` immediately.
BLOCK|hr||
BLOCK|h2|2|4. Null Coalescing (`??`)
BLOCK|p||The null coalescing operator (`??`) evaluates to the left-hand operand if it is not null/empty, or returns the fallback right-hand value otherwise:
BLOCK|code|python|// Checks if city_name is None or empty. If so, defaults to "Unknown City"
current_city := city_name ?? "Unknown City"
BLOCK|h3|3|Combining Optional Chaining & Null Coalescing
BLOCK|p||You can combine these two operators to write bulletproof, concise member access pipelines:
BLOCK|code|python|city := user?.address?.city ?? "Default City"
put city
BLOCK|p||This evaluates to the city name if the path is fully valid, or defaults safely to `"Default City"`.
BLOCK|hr||
